<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rafael Trujillo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1891–1961</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rafael Trujillo was dictator of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a> from 1930 to 1961. He rose through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-guard-dominican-republic">National Guard</a> created during the US occupation and seized power in 1930. His rule combined a personality cult, terror and personal control of the economy, and in 1937 his troops massacred thousands of Haitians. He was assassinated in 1961.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rafael-trujillo.jpg" alt="Rafael Trujillo" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rafael_L._Trujillo_en_la_silla_presidencial_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
